  "notes": "GAAP city. Governmental lines from Exhibit 4 (p4) Total Governmental Funds column; business-type from Exhibit 6 (p6) totals (receipts = operating + nonoperating revenues; interest and fees expense recorded as a disbursement). Taxes 560,307 is a combined property and city (sales) tax line with no breakdown printed (Statement of Activities: 'Property and city taxes, levied for general purposes'), kept as one 'taxes' line. The only supplementary schedule (Exhibit A-1, p8) is a combined budget-to-actual for all governmental funds, so per the per-fund rule detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds statement (General, CDBG); proprietary statement fund columns not added as detail (aligned with FY2024); budget_final null (budget figures are on another page). ending_cash = governmental funds balance sheet cash & certificates of deposit + cash county treasurer (p3); beginning cash not printed. No transfers. Statement of Activities misc revenue 8,457 vs fund statement 8,547 (not recorded as a discrepancy, different statements). Proprietary cash flow investing sign error recorded in report_discrepancies. Read pages 1-8 of 8"
}
